Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: ng pangangailangan ng better coordination

3431
03:44:41,560 --> 03:44:43,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: between NIA, Bureau of

3432
03:44:43,560 --> 03:44:45,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Soils and Water Management

3433
03:44:45,560 --> 03:44:47,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: of the DNR.

3434
03:44:47,560 --> 03:44:49,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sabi po ng mga eksperto,

3435
03:44:49,560 --> 03:44:51,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: siloed, nasa silos po

3436
03:44:51,560 --> 03:44:53,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: yung mga ahensyang ito. Ano po

3437
03:44:53,560 --> 03:44:55,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: ang ginagawa ng NIA para

3438
03:44:55,560 --> 03:44:57,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: po mas maging maayos, masinop

3439
03:44:57,560 --> 03:44:59,560
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: ang convergence when it comes to irrigation?

3440
03:45:00,000 --> 03:45:05,880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kailangan po kasi ang convergence, lalo na na naharap tayo sa isang major climate crisis, that is El Niño.

3441
03:45:07,940 --> 03:45:13,660
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Well, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Colleague, katot po na nabanggit natin kanina,

3442
03:45:14,420 --> 03:45:21,160
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: ay talaga namang walang pay, walang sawa, walang tigil din namang pinag-aaralan ng mga ahensya

3443
03:45:21,160 --> 03:45:34,640
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: na nabanggit po natin, kasama ang DA under BSWM, PHIVOLCS, DAR, NCIP, at saka ang NIA,

3444
03:45:34,920 --> 03:45:42,260
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: na talagang pinag-aaralan nila mabuti yung bagay-bagay tungkol sa patubig na nabanggit nyo,

3445
03:45:42,260 --> 03:45:47,980
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: at at dun po pala sa sinasabi nyo kanina na

3446
03:45:47,980 --> 03:45:57,480
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: na pagkakaiba ng 4.250 o yung baseline natin, may difference doon.

3447
03:45:57,620 --> 03:46:05,180
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Maski hindi nga po natin puntahan pa, Mr. Speaker, this is Colleague, yung 4 million plus na potential erigible land,

3448
03:46:05,180 --> 03:46:12,360
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: dun pa lang po tayo sa 1 million na potential ay akibat po rin talaga na malaking halaga.

3449
03:46:12,880 --> 03:46:17,960
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kaya minsan hindi na po natin sinasali po yung mas malaking figure o numero,

3450
03:46:17,980 --> 03:46:25,980
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: so kapagkat mas maganda pong mag-focus mo muna tayo dun sa original na 3.2 million hectares,

3451
03:46:26,320 --> 03:46:30,340
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: base po yun sa 3% slope, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues.

3452
03:46:30,540 --> 03:46:35,220
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, marami pong salamat sa pagtugon nyo sa mga tanong.

3453
03:46:35,220 --> 03:46:41,540
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: I cannot overemphasize the need for whole-of-government approach in addressing the challenges that is being faced

3454
03:46:41,540 --> 03:46:46,160
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: and will be faced by our farmers in the community sa pagpasok po ng El Niño.

3455
03:46:46,520 --> 03:46:47,880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Again po, inaasahan po natin.

3456
03:46:47,980 --> 03:46:53,200
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And greater convergence among government agencies in responding to the irrigation problem of our farmers.

3457
03:46:53,580 --> 03:46:56,960
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Maraming salamat po, speaker, maraming salamat, ginong sponsor.

3458
03:46:57,580 --> 03:47:00,100
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues, maraming po salamat din.

3459
03:47:01,940 --> 03:47:02,780
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: [unclear] Leader.

3460
03:47:03,560 --> 03:47:12,480
Rep. Patricia C. Calderon: Mr. Speaker, next to interpolate the sponsor, I move to recognize Representative Elijah R. San Fernando of Kamangagawa Partylist.

3461
03:47:13,480 --> 03:47:15,960
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: The Honorable San Fernando is now recognized.

3462
03:47:17,100 --> 03:47:17,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat.

3463
03:47:17,980 --> 03:47:23,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Speaker, at sa ating kaibigan, sponsor,

3464
03:47:24,840 --> 03:47:26,820
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: siing Congressman Joseph Tan.

3465
03:47:27,340 --> 03:47:29,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: May ilan lamang pong mga katanungan.

3466
03:47:32,480 --> 03:47:41,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ipagpapauna ko lang po na ang kinatawang ito ay lubos na sumusuporta sa mga proyektong pangirigasyon

3467
03:47:41,800 --> 03:47:46,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: dahil ultimately, ang makikinabang po dito ay ang ating mga magsasaka.

3468
03:47:47,980 --> 03:47:57,740
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero kaakibat po ng suporta na yan, ay dapat din po nating malaman kung nagagampanan ng National Irrigation Administration

3469
03:47:57,740 --> 03:48:07,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang kanyang napakahalagang mandato, Mr. Speaker, upang matiyak na ang mga magsasaka natin at ang kanilang mga lupang sinasaka

3470
03:48:07,100 --> 03:48:13,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay tunay na nabibigyan ng mga proyektong pangirigasyon.

3471
03:48:14,500 --> 03:48:17,240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ilan lamang pong mga clarification, Mr. Speaker.

3472
03:48:17,980 --> 03:48:23,240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At ilang mga commitments na nais makuha mula sa National Irrigation Administration.

3473
03:48:24,180 --> 03:48:36,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang hinihingi po na 46.36 billion pesos na budget for the fiscal year 2027 ng NIA

3474
03:48:36,100 --> 03:48:41,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ay kabilang po sa mga binabanggit ng People's Budget Coalition.

3475
03:48:41,300 --> 03:48:45,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ito po yung pinakamalawak na koalisyon ng mga civil society organizations.

3476
03:48:47,980 --> 03:48:58,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pinabanggit nila yung DPWH bilang mga pondong maaaring maging vulnerable sa mga tinatawag po natin ng mga insertion o mga ghost project.

3477
03:48:58,260 --> 03:49:17,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sa DPWH, meron na pong public portal kung saan makikita ang contract ID, lokasyon na may GU tag, sino ang contractor, magkano ang budget, at implementation status ng bawat proyekto.

3478
03:49:17,980 --> 03:49:35,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maari po bang mag-commit ang NIA na mag-publish din ng parehong project level data para sa lahat ng irrigation projects nito sa isang bukas at isang searchable na public portal, Mr. Speaker?

3479
03:49:35,060 --> 03:49:45,380
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues,

3480
03:49:45,380 --> 03:49:52,280
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Tama po, maganda po yung mga nabanggit ng ating butihing kasamaan dito, si Apo Eli.

3481
03:49:53,460 --> 03:50:03,600
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At maganda rin po yung mga narinig natin kanina na tungkol sa public works na meron sila mga transparency portal.

3482
03:50:03,600 --> 03:50:14,600
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At maganda rin naman kung yun ang pagkakataon po na sambitin sa kapulong ito na ang NIA rin po ngayon ay meron din po NIA transparency portal.

3483
03:50:15,380 --> 03:50:25,460
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At yun ho ay hindi, ang ibig sabihin, kasalukuyang pong binubuo yung transparency portal.

3484
03:50:25,820 --> 03:50:32,380
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At ang layunin po ay talagang maging accessible at transparent sa public ang information.

3485
03:50:33,160 --> 03:50:44,120
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Information tungkol sa irrigation, infrastructure project, at mga iba pang mga dapat natin malaman kapag meron tayong gustong makita sa ahensya, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues.

3486
03:50:44,120 --> 03:50:44,960
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Salamat po.

3487
03:50:45,380 --> 03:50:56,700
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Speaker at sa ating butihing kaibigang sponsor, binanggit po ng sponsor, Mr. Speaker, na ito ay kasalukuyang ginagawa pa o tinatapos pa.

3488
03:50:57,700 --> 03:51:11,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Meron po bang particular na petsa o timeline na sinusundan ang NIA kung kailan ilalabas itong public portal na naglalaman ng mga dokumentasyon na binanggit ng kinatawang ito?

3489
03:51:11,820 --> 03:51:14,220
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues,

3490
03:51:15,380 --> 03:51:28,380
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Ayon sa ating National Education Administration, ang ating agency, na ang timeline po nila, we hope so by the end of the year ay magkaroon na ho sila.

3491
03:51:28,700 --> 03:51:35,460
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Alam naman ho natin kasi ang kainaman ng ganitong meron tayong transparency portal.

3492
03:51:35,660 --> 03:51:43,720
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Para sa ganon ay easy access kung meron ho tayong ninanais na malaman sa procurement man o etc. etc.

3493
03:51:43,720 --> 03:51:45,220
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues.

3494
03:51:45,380 --> 03:51:50,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Salamat po, Mr. Speaker. By the end of the year po ang commitment ng NIA.

3495
03:51:51,660 --> 03:51:52,600
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: We hope so.

3496
03:51:52,800 --> 03:52:02,760
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Pero siguro mga pinakamahaba ho niyan, mga first quarter. Kasi ang procurement ho ay it takes two or three months.

3497
03:52:03,320 --> 03:52:12,240
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Pero sabi naman po nila ng ating ahensya ay pipilitin matapos nito kundi man hopefully first quarter, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues.

3498
03:52:12,520 --> 03:52:13,580
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Maasahan nyo po.

3499
03:52:13,580 --> 03:52:15,240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At least, Mr. Speaker.

3500
03:52:15,380 --> 03:52:28,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Nakakuha po tayo ng commitment sa NIA na sa katapusan ng taong ito o hanggang sa unang kwarto ng 2026 ay makakapaglabas ng transparency portal.

3501
03:52:29,160 --> 03:52:32,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mamaya po, babalikan natin yung usapin sa transparency portal.

3502
03:52:34,160 --> 03:52:40,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: May mga civil society groups po na nakikipagtulungan dito sa ating kapulungan, Mr. Speaker,

3503
03:52:40,260 --> 03:52:45,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na nananawagan na sa bawat infrastructure projects.

3504
03:52:45,380 --> 03:53:01,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Gaya ng sa DPWH ay ilabas ang BP Form 202, Program of Works, mga geotag photos at coordinates, Certificate of Implementability na pirmado ng Implementing Office,

3505
03:53:02,320 --> 03:53:06,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: LDC, PDC o Mayor's Certificate of No Objection o Support.

3506
03:53:08,060 --> 03:53:15,220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maaari rin po bang mag-commit ang NIA o meron po bang ginagawa ang NIA na kahalin tulad na ganitong mga paanagin?

3507
03:53:15,380 --> 03:53:28,480
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: May mga pamamaraan upang mapagtibay o magkaroon ng mga supporting documents doon po sa mga programa o proyektong irigasyon na pinapatupad ho ng National Irrigation Administration?

3508
03:53:29,160 --> 03:53:29,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Speaker?

3509
03:53:30,280 --> 03:53:32,120
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

3510
03:53:32,120 --> 03:53:45,120
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Tama po, no? At narinig ko nga po yung mga para malaman natin at maproteksyonan natin ang bawat salapi ng bawat ahensya ay talagang maganda pong magkaroon tayo ng nababalik.

3511
03:53:45,380 --> 03:53:47,920
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Ipanggit po ng ating butihing kasamahan po rito.

3512
03:53:48,520 --> 03:53:57,100
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At tulad ng BP202, POW, at tulad ng coordinates, at saka itong letter of no objections.

3513
03:53:57,700 --> 03:54:06,540
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Para sa ganun maiwasan po natin yung mga overlapping at alam natin specifically na dito ilalagay at hindi po saan napupunta.

3514
03:54:06,540 --> 03:54:14,960
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At asahan niyo po na ginagawin at ginagawa na rin ng ating butihing ahensya.

3515
03:54:15,380 --> 03:54:16,360
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

3516
03:54:16,360 --> 03:54:27,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, at sa ating kaibigan na sponsor, dahil muli po, on the record, nagko-commit ang NIA through the sponsor na dapat may ganitong mga klaseng supporting document

3517
03:54:27,860 --> 03:54:35,420
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: upang matiyak natin na bawat inilalaan natin na piso sa mga proyektong irigasyon ay tunay na na-implement.

3518
03:54:36,460 --> 03:54:39,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Babalikan ko rin po yung tanong na yan, Mr. Speaker.

3519
03:54:40,260 --> 03:54:43,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ngayon po, noong nakaraang budget briefing, Mr. Speaker,

3520
03:54:44,380 --> 03:54:45,360
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: binabanggit po na may...

3521
03:54:45,380 --> 03:54:54,920
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: may sinusundan na master plan at feasibility study bago mag-implement ng mga irrigation project, Mr. Speaker.

3522
03:54:55,880 --> 03:55:06,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ngayon, ito pong master plan at feasibility study, by the word itself, ito ang magiging gabay para i-address yung ilang mga importanteng katanungan.

3523
03:55:06,780 --> 03:55:13,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Halimbawa, ilan yung irrigable lands, ilan yung mga non-irrigated, ilan yung annual targets,

3524
03:55:15,380 --> 03:55:20,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kasi nagpa-plano tayo, di ba, humihingi tayo ng pondo, nagpa-plano tayo,

3525
03:55:21,300 --> 03:55:29,320
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at binanggit nga po ng ahensya na ang target pa nila ay 30% na ma-irrigate.

3526
03:55:29,460 --> 03:55:30,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tama po ba ito, Mr. Speaker?

3527
03:55:35,580 --> 03:55:38,100
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, this is colleague.

3528
03:55:38,100 --> 03:55:42,340
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yung 30% po ay base sa mga non-irrigable land pa.

3529
03:55:42,940 --> 03:55:44,100
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kasi po, kung...

3530
03:55:45,380 --> 03:55:52,280
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Titignan po natin yung pondong 3.2, ay yung land area na 3.2 million hectares.

3531
03:55:53,060 --> 03:56:01,120
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Ang 70% po nun ay na-develop na, although, andun po kasi yung sinabi natin kanina na nagkaroon po ng mga deductions

3532
03:56:01,120 --> 03:56:07,100
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: dahil sa mga housing or non-agricultural development.

3533
03:56:07,700 --> 03:56:11,080
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kaya yung 30% po na more or less 1 million hectares,

3534
03:56:12,000 --> 03:56:15,360
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: ay yun po yung kasalukuyang pinupunuan.

3535
03:56:15,380 --> 03:56:17,100
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: At yun po yung kasalukuyang pinupunuan natin na maging eligible land.

3536
03:56:17,740 --> 03:56:21,520
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Ang ka-akibat po kasing halaga na ito, pag kinuwento po natin,

3537
03:56:21,660 --> 03:56:26,700
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: ay katulad ng sinasabi nga po natin kanina, more or less, mas 1 trillion pesos.

3538
03:56:27,340 --> 03:56:28,720
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Sa pag-eco-cover po, no?

3539
03:56:28,840 --> 03:56:32,040
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: To cover the 1 million hectares.

3540
03:56:32,160 --> 03:56:32,540
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Okay po.

3541
03:56:32,840 --> 03:56:35,880
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kaya kung titignan nga po natin, no,

3542
03:56:38,880 --> 03:56:44,700
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: ay yung 600,000, mga 640 billion pesos,

3543
03:56:45,380 --> 03:56:51,380
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: yung 400,000 biyan, 2030, another 400 plus billion pesos.

3544
03:56:52,340 --> 03:56:55,160
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kung i-divide po natin sa sampuntaw nyo, more or less, mga,

3545
03:56:55,980 --> 03:56:57,480
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: o lumalabas po doon, ikwan,

3546
03:57:00,100 --> 03:57:07,980
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: lumalabas po mga more or less 160 billion pesos per year.

3547
03:57:08,360 --> 03:57:09,380
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Sampuntaw nyo yun.

3548
03:57:09,860 --> 03:57:12,360
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yun ay purely for development.

3549
03:57:13,020 --> 03:57:14,340
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Apo, Mr. Speaker.

3550
03:57:14,440 --> 03:57:15,340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

3551
03:57:15,380 --> 03:57:21,380
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, malinaw po yung targeting, no, ng National Irrigation Administration.

3552
03:57:22,280 --> 03:57:29,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And in fact, binanggit din po sa briefing na annually, nasa 1.5% ang na-accomplish ng NIA.

3553
03:57:29,960 --> 03:57:30,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tama po ba?

3554
03:57:30,860 --> 03:57:42,140
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yung hung yearly na nade-develop based doon sa graph na lumabas ho na in 10 years mula noong 2015.

3555
03:57:42,140 --> 03:57:45,140
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Kung sa tignan ho natin, yun yung increase yung 1.5%.

3556
03:57:45,380 --> 03:57:48,520
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yung 4% na napapatubigan ho natin.

3557
03:57:48,860 --> 03:57:50,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Salamat, Mr. Speaker.

3558
03:57:50,640 --> 03:57:55,600
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, ito pong tinatanong ko, Mr. Speaker, at sa ating kaibigang sponsor,

3559
03:57:56,260 --> 03:58:02,560
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: pagpapatunay lang po yan na ang NIA merong master plan na sinusundan,

3560
03:58:03,160 --> 03:58:05,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: may feasibility study na sinusundan,

3561
03:58:05,760 --> 03:58:14,480
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at malinaw sa ahensya kung saan ilalagay, ano yung ilalagay, ilan ang ilalagay.

3562
03:58:14,480 --> 03:58:15,360
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tama po ba ito?

3563
03:58:15,740 --> 03:58:24,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, doon sa sinusundang master plan, very specific, determined by the National Irrigation Administration,

3564
03:58:25,420 --> 03:58:27,760
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ilan, ano, saan ilalagay?

3565
03:58:27,960 --> 03:58:28,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Tama po, no?

3566
03:58:29,200 --> 03:58:29,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Speaker?

3567
03:58:30,220 --> 03:58:32,400
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, Mr. Colleague, tama po.

3568
03:58:32,400 --> 03:58:44,300
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yung hung tinatawag natin, yung binigay sa atin, yung una, yung National Irrigation Master Plan na dinisekho ng NIA

3569
03:58:44,300 --> 03:58:44,400
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: through...

3570
03:58:45,380 --> 03:58:52,880
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: So, Regional Irrigation Master Plan, ay doon ho natin makikita ang mga potential na area.

3571
03:58:53,780 --> 03:59:03,060
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yung paggawa ng FS, pondohan natin, at para sa ganun, alam natin na yearly, doon ho, may pattern na tayo dapat sundan.

3572
03:59:03,400 --> 03:59:04,940
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Hindi na ho yung lipad-lipad pa.

3573
03:59:05,720 --> 03:59:09,980
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Yun ho yung sa malakihang usapin, lalo tigit sa CIS, saka NIS.

3574
03:59:09,980 --> 03:59:13,980
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Pero doon ho sa mga pump-pump naman, yun ho yung pa ilan-ilan na...

3575
03:59:13,980 --> 03:59:20,620
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mas costly pa gumawa ho ng irrigation doon kung ilan lang naman ho pwedeng patubigan doon.

3576
03:59:20,720 --> 03:59:23,260
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Lalo tigit kung mataas naman ho ang slope ng lupa.

3577
03:59:23,840 --> 03:59:32,240
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Pero kung kaya naman ng mga 3% lang siya at malayong lugar, pwede na ho through pump na lang po siya.

3578
03:59:32,440 --> 03:59:33,800
Rep. Joseph S. Tan: Mr. Speaker, this is Colleague.

3579
03:59:33,800 --> 03:59:43,800
