3945
04:38:09,760 --> 04:38:10,760
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much.

3946
04:38:10,760 --> 04:38:15,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: With the indulgence po of the Honorable Speaker,

3947
04:38:16,020 --> 04:38:19,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker and distinguished colleagues in this August Chamber,

3948
04:38:20,260 --> 04:38:26,480
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I rise today and it is a distinct honor for me to sponsor the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget

3949
04:38:26,480 --> 04:38:32,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: of the Department of Agriculture, including its attached agencies and government corporations

3950
04:38:32,280 --> 04:38:35,400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: as contained in the National Expenditure Program.

3951
04:38:35,600 --> 04:38:38,300
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And the proposed budget of the Department stands at

3952
04:38:38,300 --> 04:38:41,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: 198.45 billion,

3953
04:38:41,320 --> 04:38:43,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: or about 17.25

3954
04:38:43,880 --> 04:38:51,240
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: billion, or 8% lower than the 215.69 billion appropriated last year.

3955
04:38:51,460 --> 04:38:58,460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, we enter this budget year with encouraging evidence that our investments are beginning to bear fruit.

3956
04:38:58,660 --> 04:39:07,940
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: In 2025, the Philippine Statistics Authority reported that the agriculture, forestry, and fishing sector grew by 3.1%,

3957
04:39:07,940 --> 04:39:09,860
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: reversing the 1.5%

3958
04:39:09,860 --> 04:39:12,260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: contraction recorded in 2024.

3959
04:39:13,340 --> 04:39:14,800
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And the momentum

3960
04:39:14,800 --> 04:39:16,760
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: continues to this current year.

3961
04:39:16,900 --> 04:39:24,620
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: In the second quarter alone, the value of agriculture and fisheries production increased by 2.9% year-on-year,

3962
04:39:24,740 --> 04:39:32,140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: reaching 452.22 billion at constant 2018 prices.

3963
04:39:32,540 --> 04:39:37,380
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Crops, livestock, poultry, and fisheries all reported increases in the value of production.

3964
04:39:37,400 --> 04:39:42,710
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: We have also seen concrete progress on the ground.

3965
04:39:42,720 --> 04:40:02,030
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Through programs such as Rice for All, 20 Pesos Rice, Kadiwa, enhanced buffer stocking and support provided under the Rice Tariffication Law, the government has continued to address the twin objectives of keeping food accessible to consumers while providing better support to our producers.

3966
04:40:02,040 --> 04:40:14,830
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: However, Mr. Speaker, these gains should not make us rest. This reminds us that growth in value does not automatically mean that physical production is secure.

3967
04:40:14,830 --> 04:40:25,700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: This is a central challenge before us. How do we keep food affordable for Filipino families while making farming and fishing profitable enough for Filipino producers to remain in the sector?

3968
04:40:25,740 --> 04:40:30,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: The answer cannot be found in one commodity, one agency, or one program.

3969
04:40:30,560 --> 04:40:33,840
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And it requires a complete value chain approach.

3970
04:40:34,480 --> 04:40:47,520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And this is why the 2027 budget must continue to protect the gains that we have now reached and must focus on investments that raise productivity, reduce cost, improve farm and fishery infrastructure,

3971
04:40:47,520 --> 04:40:58,460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: minimize our post-harvest losses, strengthen our cold chain and logistics systems, expand market access, improve irrigation, modernize our fisheries,

3972
04:40:58,880 --> 04:41:00,520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: strengthen animal health and biosecurity,

3973
04:41:00,560 --> 04:41:10,960
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: reduce smuggling, and make climate change resilience and disaster management and preparation part of every agricultural investment.

3974
04:41:11,520 --> 04:41:21,380
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Mr. Speaker, the proposed DA budget is smaller than last year's allocation, but the responsibilities before the department have not decreased.

3975
04:41:21,380 --> 04:41:29,520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: The department itself has emphasized that the 2027 budget must prioritize productivity, infrastructure,

3976
04:41:29,520 --> 04:41:43,640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: post-harvest systems, market access, technology, climate change, adaptation and mitigation, disaster preparedness, and stronger agricultural and fisheries value chains.

3977
04:41:44,020 --> 04:41:48,080
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: The challenge before us, therefore, is not simply how much we appropriate.

3978
04:41:48,620 --> 04:41:53,040
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: It is how much value we create from every peso that we appropriated.

3979
04:41:53,800 --> 04:41:58,950
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So every peso must translate into a hectare made more productive,

3980
04:41:58,960 --> 04:42:03,230
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: a fisherfolk family made more resilient,

3981
04:42:03,240 --> 04:42:08,920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Farmers and fisher folks' children able to go to school, a road that actually connects a farm to a market,

3982
04:42:09,380 --> 04:42:16,100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: a crop saved from post-harvest loss, animals protected from disease, smugglers caught and prosecuted,

3983
04:42:16,640 --> 04:42:26,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: a farmer protected from disaster, and a Filipino family able to buy safe and nutritious food at a reasonable price.

3984
04:42:27,080 --> 04:42:29,340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So let us not go backwards.

3985
04:42:29,520 --> 04:42:38,120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: From the gains of last year, instead, let us make the 2027 agricultural investment a forward-looking investment,

3986
04:42:38,120 --> 04:42:45,740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: not merely in production, but in productivity, profitability, resilience, and food security.

3987
04:42:46,540 --> 04:42:55,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And again, let us make our 2027 agriculture budget one that truly addresses poverty in the agricultural sector.

3988
04:42:55,760 --> 04:42:59,120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And let us make our budget able to entice younger people.

3989
04:42:59,520 --> 04:43:11,020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: We wish to build an agricultural sector where fisher folks and farmers are not simply benefiting from government programs,

3990
04:43:11,480 --> 04:43:18,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: but competitive participants and self-investors in a modern and growing economy.

3991
04:43:18,720 --> 04:43:29,340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And ultimately, let us ensure that the measures of this budget will not just be an amount today, but an investment into the future.

3992
04:43:29,520 --> 04:43:38,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So that we may have better harvests, higher income, lower losses, stronger rural communities, and more profitable farmers.

3993
04:43:38,720 --> 04:43:46,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And may that we secure food supply that all Filipinos will be able to experience today and in the future.

3994
04:43:46,920 --> 04:43:57,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And for these reasons, Mr. Speaker, I respectfully urge this honorable house to support the proposed 2027 budget of the Department of Agriculture

3995
04:43:58,520 --> 04:44:02,310
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and its attached agencies and corporations.

3996
