Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker. Magre-request po ang kinatawa na ito ng kopya ng report

4045
04:48:41,400 --> 04:48:47,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: once available pag ito po ay naitapos na by end of September. Mr. Speaker, good sponsor,

4046
04:48:47,980 --> 04:48:55,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang sunod na lang po nating tanong ay tungkol po sa mga datos na binahagi ng DA nung nakaraang

4047
04:48:56,300 --> 04:49:03,340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na budget briefing. Kung saan nakita din po dito na sa ilalim ng Magna Carta for Agricultural

4048
04:49:03,340 --> 04:49:10,880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Workers at ng RA 8435, obligado rin ang gobyerno na protektahan ng prime agricultural lands.

4049
04:49:10,880 --> 04:49:19,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At magsasagawa ayon sa pangako ng DA na magpapatupad ng geofencing policy upang ihinto ang encroachment

4050
04:49:19,620 --> 04:49:26,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng mga solar power infrastructures sa 3 million hectares ng prime agricultural lands. Mr.

4051
04:49:26,300 --> 04:49:32,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Speaker, good sponsor, ano na po na yung legal status ng nasabing gagawing geofencing policy guidelines?

4052
04:49:32,740 --> 04:49:50,740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Rest assured that upon conferring with the secretary, geofencing will be completed by the end of December.

4053
04:49:51,340 --> 04:49:54,200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: End of December po, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

4054
04:49:54,200 --> 04:49:56,200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

4055
04:49:56,300 --> 04:50:07,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At maaari po bang mapaliwanag kung bakit po up to December pa yung pagsagawa ng geofencing policy guidelines?

4056
04:50:08,420 --> 04:50:17,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Meron po bang pagtukoy ng mga prime agricultural lands kung bakit ito po ay magtatagal all the way to 3 months from now?

4057
04:50:20,740 --> 04:50:26,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: First of all, we can't just, Mr. Speaker, we need to give you validated data.

4058
04:50:26,300 --> 04:50:30,260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And it will take us time to validate.

4059
04:50:30,760 --> 04:50:37,700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Actually, yung ibang prime agricultural lands ay underwater pa due to the massive flooding.

4060
04:50:38,020 --> 04:50:44,100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, there's actually a lot of validation that cannot go on at this point because of natural disasters.

4061
04:50:44,260 --> 04:50:48,080
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, we're waiting for things to settle down upon which we will validate ASAP.

4062
04:50:49,800 --> 04:50:51,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

4063
04:50:51,940 --> 04:50:56,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: As a final confirmation, para po.

4064
04:50:56,300 --> 04:51:01,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa pagtukoy kung paano nakakatuwang ang DA sa usaping land reform,

4065
04:51:01,620 --> 04:51:11,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ano po ba ang strategy o legal framework ng DA upang tiyakin na hindi mailalabas sa agricultural classification ang mga natitirang sakahan?

4066
04:51:11,880 --> 04:51:24,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ito po ay pagkatapos ibahagi yung data point last budget briefing na ang average farm size in the Philippines is only around 3.59 to 2.03 hectares.

4067
04:51:24,060 --> 04:51:26,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, given na nga na kakaunti sila.

4068
04:51:26,300 --> 04:51:33,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At syempre kakaunti pa yung may ganitong democratic na paghatian ng mga agricultural lands,

4069
04:51:34,160 --> 04:51:40,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: paano po natin may ensure na hindi mailalabas sa agricultural classification ang mga natitirang sakahan?

4070
04:51:41,180 --> 04:51:47,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lalo na, kinikilala po ba ng DA na mismong kawalan ng land security ng ating mga magsasaka

4071
04:51:47,980 --> 04:51:54,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang pangunahing dahilan ng kawalan ng pambansang agricultural productivity and food security?

4072
04:51:54,420 --> 04:51:55,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

4073
04:51:56,300 --> 04:51:57,980
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

4074
04:51:58,700 --> 04:52:05,260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And that is really a major concern of the Department of Agriculture, is how to preserve the remaining agricultural lands.

4075
04:52:05,640 --> 04:52:09,400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And as we know, there are a lot of areas that are rapidly industrializing.

4076
04:52:10,680 --> 04:52:14,580
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: One of the things that we need to do is, there are actually a two-pronged approach.

4077
04:52:14,960 --> 04:52:17,640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: One is to provide value to agricultural lands.

4078
04:52:18,020 --> 04:52:26,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And the way to do this is to make them more productive, and not only to increase production, but to increase profitability.

4079
04:52:26,300 --> 04:52:34,760
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Because if all farmers are making a profit from their land, then they would not be so quick to sell them to other persons.

4080
04:52:35,220 --> 04:52:37,760
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So number one is production and profitability.

4081
04:52:38,460 --> 04:52:46,140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So the DA is trying to increase its production, and hopefully also through reduction of post-harvest losses,

4082
04:52:46,460 --> 04:52:55,900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: proper irrigation, support for fertilizers and pesticides, and the proper prices, farm gate prices,

4083
04:52:56,300 --> 04:53:03,920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: then farmers will be able to make a living, and will not be tempted to sell their lots to speculators and developers.

4084
04:53:04,460 --> 04:53:06,800
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Secondly, that's the approach towards the farmer.

4085
04:53:07,180 --> 04:53:09,540
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: There also needs to be an approach towards developers.

4086
04:53:10,120 --> 04:53:15,660
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And one of the ways that the DA can do this is to work with the LGUs to discuss conversion.

4087
04:53:15,660 --> 04:53:23,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: There should be strict rules and guidelines, and if necessary, to even put conversion moratoriums,

4088
04:53:23,880 --> 04:53:25,660
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: so that developers will not be able to just...

4089
04:53:26,300 --> 04:53:26,820
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Convert.

4090
04:53:27,340 --> 04:53:32,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And destroy, unfortunately, irrigated land, which has happened very frequently.

4091
04:53:33,160 --> 04:53:35,160
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So I would say, there would be a two-pronged approach.

4092
04:53:35,160 --> 04:53:43,260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: To raise value for the farmers, so that they won't sell their land, and number two, is to put a stop to conversion,

4093
04:53:43,260 --> 04:53:47,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and unfortunately, destroying irrigated land.

4094
04:53:48,060 --> 04:53:55,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Touching on doon po sa nabukas na isang prong, and subprong neto, no,

4095
04:53:55,160 --> 04:53:55,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: No.

4096
04:53:55,660 --> 04:53:56,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: No.

4097
04:53:56,160 --> 04:54:03,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: naaalagaan yung kapakanan ng ating mga magsasaka at yung usaping profitability na ang reality,

4098
04:54:04,040 --> 04:54:13,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: tama nga po ang narinig natin sa ating good sponsor, marami pong mga magsasaka natin ang napapwersa na ibenta yung kanilang lupa

4099
04:54:13,520 --> 04:54:20,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: dahil hindi profitable generally yung kanilang pagsasaka for many reasons.

4100
04:54:20,360 --> 04:54:31,580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: To the point nga po na batay din po sa nakaraang hearing, ang agricultural sector ay may 10.44 million registered workers na lang sa RSVSA

4101
04:54:31,580 --> 04:54:41,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na sa 20% ng kabuo ang lakas paggawa ng bansa pero 7.9% lang ang ambag sa GDP at mababa ang youth participation rate.

4102
04:54:41,080 --> 04:54:50,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Hindi po mataas yung bilang ng mga tuloy-tuloy na nakakapag-replenish ng mga participants in the agricultural sector

4103
04:54:50,360 --> 04:54:55,460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at mga mga cultural industry with an average age of 56 years old.

4104
04:54:56,240 --> 04:55:02,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Isang bahagi po niyan yung framework by which paano po natin naaabot yung assistance.

4105
04:55:03,080 --> 04:55:12,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung saan, more often than not, it would be loan assistance instead na magkaroon ng direct non-collateral production subsidies.

4106
04:55:12,620 --> 04:55:18,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang tanong po natin, Mr. Speaker Good Sponsor, naiintindihan naman natin na merong mga subsidies

4107
04:55:18,020 --> 04:55:30,000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero may kadalasan na one-time labas lang po ito versus yung mas available at unfortunately mas nakakalubog na loan assistance.

4108
04:55:30,340 --> 04:55:34,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Bakit po nananatili na ganito ang framework ng DA?

4109
04:55:35,360 --> 04:55:41,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Higher dependence on loan assistance instead of direct non-collateral production subsidies.

4110
04:55:41,520 --> 04:55:42,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

4111
04:55:48,020 --> 04:55:57,300
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you for that inquiry, Mr. Speaker.

4112
04:55:57,300 --> 04:56:04,640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And it does not necessarily mean that if you give credit, then credit is worse than giving direct assistance.

4113
04:56:06,020 --> 04:56:17,640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So the DA continues, especially for the rice program, the DA continues to give assistance in terms of seeds, hybrid seeds and inbred seeds through the National Rice Program.

4114
04:56:18,020 --> 04:56:19,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And the RCEP program.

4115
04:56:19,800 --> 04:56:22,960
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: The DA also continues to support with fertilizers.

4116
04:56:22,960 --> 04:56:30,400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: The DA has also given diesel assistance, especially nung tumaas po ang presyo ng diesel.

4117
04:56:30,980 --> 04:56:34,980
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And the DA has also continued to give marketing assistance.

4118
04:56:35,780 --> 04:56:41,200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So the DA continues to give assistance, direct assistance to farmers.

4119
04:56:41,760 --> 04:56:47,100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: But again, there is nothing wrong also with giving access to credit.

4120
04:56:48,020 --> 04:56:54,260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: We also want people to become enterprises and not to become dependent on the government alone.

4121
04:56:54,260 --> 04:57:18,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So we want them to be able to graduate actually from assistance, hopefully, and eventually establish themselves as strong, independent, financially stable cooperatives and irrigators associations who are with the proper farm gate prices, very profitable, and able to enter into contracts with the government.

4122
04:57:18,000 --> 04:57:19,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And non-government entities.

4123
04:57:20,460 --> 04:57:23,680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And to be able to be strong and stable businesses.

4124
04:57:24,380 --> 04:57:27,180
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So it's not that we're going to support them forever.

4125
04:57:27,600 --> 04:57:36,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: But the DA also has a framework upon which they get those cooperatives and irrigators associations which are not yet mature.

4126
04:57:36,760 --> 04:57:47,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: They educate them, give them trainings, give them assistance in terms of mechanization, seeds, fertilizers, until such point that they become matured.

4127
04:57:48,000 --> 04:57:54,860
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: They become profitable, hopefully, with the proper farm gate prices and able to stand on their own, able to take on loans.

4128
04:57:54,860 --> 04:58:11,060
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: There's nothing wrong with taking on a loan, especially if you know that your cooperative or that your irrigators association will be able to project a good income for the next 5, 3, 5, 8, 10 years and be able to support the loan that you have taken.

4129
04:58:11,740 --> 04:58:17,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, yes, it's good that the DA is giving us subsidies and credit.

4130
04:58:17,000 --> 04:58:17,900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And together.

4131
04:58:18,000 --> 04:58:27,520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: They will help us build strong, mature, and financially capable farmers who are working together to become profitable and to produce adequate food supply.

4132
04:58:28,280 --> 04:58:29,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

4133
04:58:30,260 --> 04:58:43,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa dulo naman po nito, ang pinangahawakan po nating mga accounts, kung bakit natin binubukas ito, ay sa pagkukonsulta sa mga magsasaka, ang kalimitan na inuulat nila dalawa po.

4134
04:58:43,860 --> 04:58:47,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung usapin po na kung sila po ay maaaring.

4135
04:58:48,000 --> 04:59:01,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung makapagkuha ng mga direct subsidies, kalimitan kung may listahan yan, nahihirapan sila o magugulat na lang sila na hindi po sila maka-include dito sa listahan na ito.

4136
04:59:01,160 --> 04:59:17,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And syempre, ang mas available na method na assistance kung hindi po maka-avail ng gano'n ay yung sa loan na yun nga po, sa puno't dulo po nito, kung dito po nakakapag-default na paano ma...

4137
04:59:18,000 --> 04:59:38,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: i-uplift ng mga magsasaka ang kanilang kahirapan sa ngayon at ito po ay sisingilin pa ng mas malaki sa mga susunod na mga taon, ay hindi rin po nakakapag-encourage na magpanatili sa agricultural industry now that we've seen that mga ilang taon po ang ganitong nagawa.

4138
04:59:38,360 --> 04:59:47,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And unfortunately, hindi po siya naka-entice sa mga kabataan o kaya naman sa mga tagamana ng mga sakahan.

4139
04:59:48,000 --> 04:59:52,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kaya magpanatili ng ganitong klaseng pag-participasyon sa industriya.

4140
04:59:53,100 --> 05:00:00,000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang huling tanong na lang po siguro, Madam Speaker, ay Mr. Speaker, Gunsponsor, paano po ba natin may imbitahan ang mga may...

4141
05:00:00,000 --> 05:00:02,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na pumasok sa agricultural sector.

4142
05:00:02,800 --> 05:00:04,280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung may ganitong mga policies,

4143
05:00:04,720 --> 05:00:05,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: nasa punot-dulo po nito,

4144
05:00:06,420 --> 05:00:12,600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang pinaka-question ay hindi po sa kanila,

4145
05:00:13,400 --> 05:00:14,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: hindi nila pagmamayari.

4146
05:00:14,680 --> 05:00:17,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yung sariling lupa, kalimitan, ay kailangan pong upahan.

4147
05:00:17,140 --> 05:00:22,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And of course, may limitation yung makikita at maaasaan

4148
05:00:22,260 --> 05:00:24,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: sa direct financial and production shields.

4149
05:00:24,380 --> 05:00:38,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Paano na lang po may imbitahan ng mga mamamayan

4150
05:00:38,760 --> 05:00:41,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na pumasok sa agriculture or bumalik sa agricultural industry

4151
05:00:41,900 --> 05:00:45,200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: given po yung mga iba't-ibang mga issues na na-raise, Mr. Speaker?

4152
05:00:45,260 --> 05:00:46,140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

4153
05:00:46,260 --> 05:00:47,980
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: There is only one answer to this.

4154
05:00:48,760 --> 05:00:51,900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Pag kumikita po, dudumugin po yan ang mga tao.

4155
05:00:52,460 --> 05:00:54,120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Di ba, there is a saying na,

4156
05:00:54,680 --> 05:00:57,800
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: pag nagtayo ka na isang business at kumita si business,

4157
05:00:58,420 --> 05:01:01,300
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: the next day, parang kabuti na yung mga kapitbahay mo,

4158
05:01:01,680 --> 05:01:03,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: pareho na yung business nyo.

4159
05:01:03,300 --> 05:01:05,620
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So there's only one answer actually to that.

4160
05:01:05,700 --> 05:01:07,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And if it is profitable,

4161
05:01:07,180 --> 05:01:11,740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: then therefore, so many people will rush there and start farming.

4162
05:01:12,080 --> 05:01:15,740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: But while it continues to be unprofitable with low farmgate prices,

4163
05:01:16,120 --> 05:01:17,820
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: difficult access to market,

4164
05:01:18,300 --> 05:01:20,440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: difficult access to direct buyers,

4165
05:01:20,840 --> 05:01:23,140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: then there will not be enough persons

4166
05:01:23,140 --> 05:01:24,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: who want to enter,

4167
05:01:24,380 --> 05:01:25,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: who want to enter agriculture.

4168
05:01:25,780 --> 05:01:26,340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And secondly,

4169
05:01:26,800 --> 05:01:29,840
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: though I would say that profitability is the number one reason

4170
05:01:29,840 --> 05:01:31,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: that people would enter agriculture,

4171
05:01:32,140 --> 05:01:34,520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and there are so many ways to make this profitable.

4172
05:01:34,760 --> 05:01:37,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: One of these is through proper irrigation.

4173
05:01:38,620 --> 05:01:41,200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Dati po sa amin, we only used to have one cropping.

4174
05:01:41,520 --> 05:01:42,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: With the coming of the UPRIS,

4175
05:01:42,980 --> 05:01:45,300
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: the Upper Pampanga River Irrigation System,

4176
05:01:45,740 --> 05:01:49,340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: they went from one cropping to three croppings.

4177
05:01:50,200 --> 05:01:53,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So after that, so many people started to plant again.

4178
05:01:53,320 --> 05:01:54,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So profitability,

4179
05:01:54,920 --> 05:01:57,640
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: but another reason that I would like to give you is culture.

4180
05:01:58,260 --> 05:02:01,660
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: We need to change the culture of Filipinos.

4181
05:02:02,180 --> 05:02:03,100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Farming is honorable,

4182
05:02:03,420 --> 05:02:04,420
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: farming is profitable,

4183
05:02:04,960 --> 05:02:07,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: at nakita po natin noong COVID-19,

4184
05:02:07,440 --> 05:02:10,380
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: sino ho ba ang sumikat kung hindi po mga magsasaka?

4185
05:02:10,760 --> 05:02:12,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And there was even a saying on FB na,

4186
05:02:13,440 --> 05:02:17,160
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: eto po yung dumating na araw na mas mahalaga pala ang bukid kesa sa mall.

4187
05:02:17,740 --> 05:02:19,680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So we need also to change the culture.

4188
05:02:19,840 --> 05:02:24,240
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Farming is not for persons who have not gone to school,

4189
05:02:24,640 --> 05:02:27,680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: who are, that is the last option in their life.

4190
05:02:28,100 --> 05:02:31,120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Farming should be a first option of persons who own land.

4191
05:02:31,540 --> 05:02:33,700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: To own land is to be a wealthy person

4192
05:02:33,700 --> 05:02:36,860
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: because you have collateral in whatever you do.

4193
05:02:37,280 --> 05:02:40,340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: But if you don't have land, you are not a wealthy person.

4194
05:02:40,340 --> 05:02:43,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi po, wala po kayong maipreprenda pag meron nung may sakit.

4195
05:02:44,500 --> 05:02:50,740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: At wala po kayong, that farming in your land is an extra backup po sa pamilya.

4196
05:02:51,180 --> 05:02:54,300
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So again, make it profitable.

4197
05:02:54,380 --> 05:02:56,700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And number two, make it honorable.

4198
05:02:57,280 --> 05:03:00,440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And you will have, do dumugin po tayo ng mga magsasaka.

4199
05:03:00,920 --> 05:03:02,960
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: All below the age of 30.

4200
05:03:03,780 --> 05:03:04,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

4201
05:03:05,100 --> 05:03:09,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I'd love to buy in to the vision of the distinguished sponsor here.

4202
05:03:09,580 --> 05:03:15,340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Unfortunately, yung nakikita po natin na issue ng profitability ay napakahirap

4203
05:03:15,340 --> 05:03:23,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: dahil po hindi nga po makasurvive ang isang farmer given yung state of the market ngayon.

4204
05:03:23,440 --> 05:03:24,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Hindi lang po.

4205
05:03:24,380 --> 05:03:33,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ito issue siyempre ng paano po nakakapagset ng prices dito sa mga produce na ginagawa ng ating mga farmers.

4206
05:03:33,180 --> 05:03:40,280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero napapwersa silang makipagkumpetensya sa iba't ibang mga imports na pumapasok at pinaflood yung markets natin.

4207
05:03:40,620 --> 05:03:49,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At ngayon po may mga batas po tayo na rather than mas protektahan kung paano makakapagbigay ng pagkain at ng input

4208
05:03:49,260 --> 05:03:53,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng galing sa farmers natin sa iba't ibang merkado dito sa ating bansa.

4209
05:03:54,020 --> 05:03:54,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Na may...

4210
05:03:54,380 --> 05:03:55,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May goal for export, diba?

4211
05:03:55,940 --> 05:04:02,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang mas na-encourage po ay paano mag-import at paano mas ma-welcome yung mas mababang presyo ng import dito sa ating bansa.

4212
05:04:02,260 --> 05:04:06,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yun naman po yung nakita natin, narinig din natin from the Department of Agriculture before

4213
05:04:06,540 --> 05:04:13,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and compounding issues po ito kung bakit mas nahihirapan ang mga magsasaka natin at nahihirapan silang mag-maintain sa industriya.

4214
05:04:13,940 --> 05:04:19,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Nonetheless, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, ang ending naman po nito ay kailangan po may pagbabago sa ating batas.

4215
05:04:19,640 --> 05:04:24,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung saan yung rice importation and dependence po.

4216
05:04:24,380 --> 05:04:31,280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa ating agricultural imports, bayak, ng iba't ibang produce ay kailangan na pong matanggal.

4217
05:04:31,740 --> 05:04:37,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At syempre, yung genuine agrarian land reform ay kailangan na rin pong matrabaho, hindi lang sa batas,

4218
05:04:37,800 --> 05:04:43,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: pero paano po ito mabibigyan ng pangil ang Department of Agriculture and Department of Agrarian Reform na gawin.

4219
05:04:44,100 --> 05:04:46,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For now, Mr. Speaker, I no longer have any further questions.

4220
05:04:46,880 --> 05:04:47,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you for the time.

4221
05:04:48,180 --> 05:04:49,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: To the distinguished sponsor.

4222
05:04:49,760 --> 05:04:50,680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much, po.

